  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Other communications tasks as agreed upon by the client\" is an unbounded catch-all closing a list of specific services, so its reach against the enumerated items is uncertain. Whether such tasks fall inside the retainer or outside the Scope of Services turns on this phrase.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
    {"issue": "This open-ended item cannot easily be squared with section 1.2, which charges services \"that fall outside the boundaries of the Scope of Services\" at hourly rates; work agreed under \"Other Tasks\" is simultaneously inside and outside the scope. The boundary between the two provisions is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Xenophon's then-currently hourly rates\" refers to a rate schedule that appears nowhere in the Agreement, and the phrase is itself garbled. \"[S]uch as public affairs campaigns\" gives one example for an otherwise unbounded category of \"[a]dditional services\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
    {"issue": "This hourly-rate billing regime sits against section 4.1, which fixes a $30,000 monthly retainer for the scope of work, and against 1.1's \"Other Tasks\" catch-all; nothing identifies which regime applies to a given task. The Agreement contains no rate card to make 1.2 operable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[W]ill be on-going\" fixes no term or end date, leaving the duration of performance indeterminate; the section is also misnumbered 2.4 in an Article whose only other section is 2.2. The absence of any 2.1 or 2.3 compounds the uncertainty about what was intended.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
    {"issue": "An \"on-going\" period of performance must be read with section 2.2, which permits either party to terminate on 60 days' notice; whether the contract is perpetual or terminable at will is left to be harmonised.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[T]erminated by either party with 60-days written notice\" does not say when notice is effective, whether the retainer accrues through the notice period, or what happens to work in progress. The measure of \"60-days\" against the monthly billing cycle is unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
    {"issue": "This right to terminate must be reconciled with section 2.4's \"on-going\" period of performance and with section 6.1, which lets the Client stop all work while still paying \"in accordance with the terms and provisions of this Agreement\". Whether stopping work under 6.1 avoids the 60-day notice is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[W]ill include but is not limited to\" names six individuals while disclaiming that the list is exhaustive, so the staffing commitment has no ascertainable content. Nothing states any minimum involvement by the named personnel.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18},
